From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: bcmbca: add SMP support for CFE booted Cortex-A7 SoCs

Broadcom CFE on BCM47622 / BCM6755 doesn't provide PSCI. Secondary cores
are parked in WFI and jump to the address stored in the GPIO
"GeneralPurpose" register once they receive an SGI. Add a "brcm,bca-smp"
enable-method implementing that protocol with a holding pen, similar to
the one used by the vendor kernel.

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-bcm/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-bcm/Makefile
@@ -60,4 +60,5 @@
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_ARCH_BCMBCA),y)
 obj-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_BCMBCA)	+= board_bcmbca.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SMP)		+= bcm63xx_smp.o bcm63xx_pmb.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SMP)		+= bcmbca_smp.o bcmbca_headsmp.o
 endif
